<title>ITALY: Giovanni Agnelli e C. Sapa net profit up 8 pct.</title>
<headline>Giovanni Agnelli e C. Sapa net profit up 8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Giovanni Agnelli e C. Sapa, the limited share partnership which holds 82.5 percent of ordinary shares in holding company IFI which controls Fiat Spa, posted a net profit of 20.9 billion lire in the year to October 31, up 8.0 percent on the previous period.</p>
<p>The company, which acts as the &quot;Agnelli family's &quot;treasure chest&quot;, said it will distribute dividends totalling 17 billion lire, against 19.4 billion lire in the 1994/95 year.</p>
<p>A statement said shareholders would be asked to approve a three year extension of the chairmanship of Giovanni Agnelli who is also Fiat honorary chairman.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
